WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.290
Who should sort the envelopes?

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.044
Most pipelines send every job to the same frontier model.

00:00:06.144 --> 00:00:08.718
An agent writes, and it decides.

00:00:09.918 --> 00:00:13.342
A gate asks one narrow question per item.

00:00:13.392 --> 00:00:18.924
When it is confident, cheap code handles it. When it is unsure, the main model does.

00:00:19.474 --> 00:00:28.287
Four tools, in rising order of cost. Rules. A classic classifier. A small L L M.

00:00:28.337 --> 00:00:30.088
And a System One model.

00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:33.412
Every answer carries a confidence score.

00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:37.340
The gate is allowed to be ignorant, it is not allowed to guess.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.880
In early tests on roughly eighteen and a half thousand emails,

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:46.344
a method from two thousand three scored ninety-eight point four percent.

00:00:46.394 --> 00:00:48.696
Jev scored ninety-eight point three.

00:00:49.246 --> 00:00:55.831
Before any vendor, label two hundred real examples. Train a basic classifier.

00:00:55.881 --> 00:00:58.629
Measure it. Then wire it in.

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:01.900
Nothing enters the pipeline until it beats that baseline.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.760
That's module three, the gate. Start with page one: Cheap Decisions.
